\caption(The sixteen logical bits occupy one 64-bit word: eight payload bytes including padding. Logical bit count and allocated payload are separate quantities.)

> Deriving the sizing approximation

Under independent uniform placement, one fixed bit remains clear after kn
placements with probability \((1-1/m)^{kn}\). Approximating this by
\(e^{-kn/m}\), and treating the k queried bits as independent, gives

$$
p_{\rm model}=\left(1-e^{-kn/m}\right)^k.
$$
\alttext(The model false-positive probability is one minus the exponential of minus k n over m, all raised to k.)

The first finite-placement marginal is exact under that placement model. Raising
the fill probability to k adds an independence approximation; it is not an exact
finite-filter probability. Deterministic double hashing, repeated positions and
string-key distributions add further departures. Here n means distinct keys,
not repeated calls to add; the filter does not store an insertion count.

Writing \(r=m/n\) and \(t=k/r\), differentiation of the model's log gives
\(\log(1-e^{-t})+t/(e^t-1)=0\), with its minimum at t=ln(2).
Thus the continuous rule is

$$
k_*=(m/n)\log 2,\qquad
p_*\approx\exp\!\left[-(m/n)(\log 2)^2\right].
$$
\alttext(The model-optimal continuous hash count is m over n times the natural logarithm of two. The corresponding model error is the exponential of minus m over n times the square of that logarithm.)

The API rounds that k to an integer and clamps it to at least one; for an empty
design load it returns one. This is a sizing rule, not an exact optimisation for
the implemented wrapped probes. The model calculation uses `expm1` to avoid
subtracting nearly equal numbers at light load.

> Original experiment: 1,000 strings and 5,000 absent probes

Retain m=8,000, target n=1,000, rounded k=6, and ten batches of 100 inserted
strings key0,...,key999. Each batch queries the same 5,000 different absent
strings absent0,...,absent4999. Those are deterministic synthetic inputs;
fractions describe this probe set and do not certify a population error rate.
Reusing probes across batches also correlates the displayed measurements.

The original string helper used a nonstandard FNV offset basis. It is now
standard 64-bit FNV-1a, verified against RFC 9923 vectors including trailing NUL
bytes. String hashes and these observed counts therefore change; applications
retaining hashes from the old helper must rebuild them. The probe mapping for
already supplied integer keys is unchanged.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bloom_load.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  using dm::algorithms::bloom_hash64;
  const int k=dm::algorithms::BloomFilter::optimal_num_hashes(8000,1000);
  dm::algorithms::BloomFilter filter(8000,k);
  std::vector<double> load,observed,model;
  std::print("m = {}; k = {}; payload = {} bytes; absent probes per batch = 5000.\n\n",
             filter.num_bits(),k,filter.storage_bytes());
  std::print("| distinct inserts | false positives / 5000 | observed fraction | model fraction | set bits |\n"
             "| ---: | :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (int batch=0;batch<10;++batch) {
    for (int i=0;i<100;++i) filter.add(bloom_hash64("key"+std::to_string(batch*100+i)));
    const int n=(batch+1)*100;int fp=0;
    for (int i=0;i<5000;++i) fp+=filter.maybe_contains(bloom_hash64("absent"+std::to_string(i)));
    for (int i=0;i<n;++i) if (!filter.maybe_contains(bloom_hash64("key"+std::to_string(i)))) return 1;
    const double measured=fp/5000.,predicted=filter.expected_false_positive_rate(n);
    load.push_back(n);observed.push_back(measured);model.push_back(predicted);
    std::print("| {} | {} / 5000 | {:.6f} | {:.6f} | {} |\n",n,fp,measured,predicted,filter.num_set_bits());
  }
  const double ymax=1.6*std::max(*std::max_element(observed.begin(),observed.end()),model.back());
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .points(load,observed,"observed",dm::RGB{37,99,235},5)
      .lines(load,model,"model",dm::RGB{220,38,38},2)
      .title("Fixed absent probes as an 8000-bit filter fills")
      .x_label("distinct inserted strings").y_label("false-positive fraction")
      .y_limits(0,ymax).size(900,480).save_svg("build/bloom_load.svg");
}
```
